  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Business Performance of Micro-Small and Medium Sized Enterprises (MSMEs) in Post-Conflict Areas in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Multi-Donor Action &#x201c;Support for the Recovery of Micro Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) in Post-Conflict Areas in Ethiopia&#x201d; is jointly co-financed by the European Union, the German Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ), and the Ministry for Foreign Trade and Development Cooperation of the Netherlands. Outcome 2 (henceforth in this document referred to as &#x201c;the (Joint) Action&#x201d; on the proposal) is implemented by the GIZ GmbH. It is scheduled from 01.10.2023 to 30.09.2027 (48 months) with a total budget of 7,000 ,000 (EU contribution EUR 1,000,000, BMZ contribution EUR 3,000,000, the EKN contribution EUR 3,000,000). The Overall Objective of the Action is: To restore the local economy and build the resilience of MSMEs that are affected by the crises in Ethiopia, with a focus on the North of the Country. The Specific Objective (Outcome) 2 of the Action is: The business performance of MSME is improved.</narrative>
  </description>
